{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"GGUF\/SafeTensors Parsing & Sampling","modules":[{"name":"SwiftLLM"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderInference","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalShadersQuantization"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftLLM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides high-throughput binary weight parsers that map model weights directly into unified memory (UMA) without intermediate memory allocations, paired with a robust token sampling pipeline operating strictly on unnormalized logits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"1-GGUF-Zero-Copy-Weight-Parsing","level":2,"text":"1. GGUF Zero-Copy Weight Parsing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"GGUFParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" decodes GGUF header metadata and extracts tensor blocks into semantic ","type":"text"},{"code":"QuantizedTensor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" representations without eager dequantization into full floating-point arrays:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Foundation","import SwiftLLM","","let modelURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"models\/llama-3-8b-instruct.Q4_0.gguf\")","","\/\/ 1. Parse GGUF weights into QuantizedTensor map","let weights: [String: QuantizedTensor] = try GGUFParser.parse(url: modelURL)","","\/\/ 2. Inspect parsed tensor metadata","if let attnWeight = weights[\"blk.0.attn_q.weight\"] {","    print(\"Tensor name: \\(attnWeight.name)\")","    print(\"Shape: \\(attnWeight.shape)\")","    print(\"Scheme: \\(String(describing: attnWeight.scheme))\") \/\/ .q4_0","    print(\"Block Size: \\(attnWeight.layoutMetadata.blockSize)\") \/\/ 32","}","","\/\/ 3. Extract separated packed weight and scale buffers for Metal GEMV","if let (packedWeights, scales) = weights[\"blk.0.attn_q.weight\"]?.extractSeparatedBuffers() {","    print(\"Extracted \\(packedWeights.count) weight bytes and \\(scales.count) scale bytes.\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"2-SafeTensors-Zero-Copy-Weight-Parsing","level":2,"text":"2. SafeTensors Zero-Copy Weight Parsing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"SafeTensorsParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parses JSON header descriptors and maps FP16\/FP32\/BF16 tensor payloads directly into ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLXArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Foundation","import SwiftLLM","import MLX","","let safeURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"models\/model.safetensors\")","","\/\/ Parse SafeTensors into native MLX tensor dictionary","let tensors: [String: MLXArray] = try SafeTensorsParser.parse(url: safeURL)","","for (tensorName, array) in tensors {","    print(\"Loaded tensor '\\(tensorName)': shape=\\(array.shape), dtype=\\(array.dtype)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"3-Token-Sampling-with-SamplingConfiguration","level":2,"text":"3. Token Sampling with SamplingConfiguration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"After computing next-token logits from ","type":"text"},{"code":"TransformerDecoder.forward","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", token selection is governed by ","type":"text"},{"code":"SamplingConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftLLM","import MLX","","\/\/ 1. Define generation parameters","let sampling = SamplingConfiguration(","    temperature: 0.7,","    topK: 40,","    topP: 0.9,","    repetitionPenalty: 1.1",")","","let pastTokens = [128000, 791, 7453, 374]","let nextLogits: MLXArray = ... \/\/ Shape [vocab_size] from decoder.forward","","\/\/ 2. Sample next token ID applying penalty, temperature, top-k, and top-p","let nextToken = Sampler.sample(","    logits: nextLogits,","    config: sampling,","    pastTokens: pastTokens",")","","print(\"Sampled next token ID: \\(nextToken)\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[!TIP]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For detailed mathematical formulations of repetition penalty, temperature scaling, top-k truncation, and nucleus (top-p) masking, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"type":"thematicBreak"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftllm\/weightparsingandsampling"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/GGUFParser","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SafeTensorsParser","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedTensor","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLayoutMetadata"],"title":"Weight Parsers & Representations","anchor":"Weight-Parsers--Representations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/Sampler","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingConfiguration","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/LLMOptions","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies"],"title":"Sampling & Decoding","anchor":"Sampling--Decoding"}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Parse GGUF and SafeTensors model weights zero-copy into Apple Silicon unified memory and sample tokens with f